{
 "version": 1,
 "name": "cow",
 "archetype": "creature.quadruped",
 "description": "A dairy cow in Holstein proportions: a deep lofted barrel with hooks and pins, a thick neck with a dewlap, a long head carried low with a broad pink muzzle, nostrils, eyes and sideways ears, irregular black (or red) patches on a white coat that follow the body, an udder with four teats, legs with knees, hocks that bend backwards and hooves, and a long tail with a switch. Horns are an option (most dairy cows are dehorned). Legs, knees, hocks, head and tail are nodes with their pivot at the joint. Head towards +Z, hooves on y = 0.",
